# Migrations belong to scripts/graphify/sql_layer.py, which mints ONE node per
# database object (db_tbl_*, db_fn_*, …) across all 227 migrations. graphify's
# own SQL extractor (tree-sitter-sql) mints one node per object PER FILE, so a
# table touched by 30 migrations would appear 30 times next to its real node.
# Other .sql files (supabase/tests, seed, audits, scripts) are still parsed.
supabase/migrations/
# Superseded by the 2026-07-02 re-baseline; parsing it would answer "where is
# this defined?" with migrations that no longer describe the database.
supabase/migrations_archive_pre_baseline_20260702/
# Superseded by the 2026-10-13 re-baseline (docs/operations/database-baseline.md).
supabase/migrations_archive_pre_baseline_20261013/
